From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:07:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [voicecall] Say whether a call is carried over IMS.

A handler's isIms is true for a call that goes over IMS (VoLTE, VoNR,
VoWiFi) rather than the circuit-switched network. The oFono provider
reads it from libqofono's QOfonoVoiceCall::ims, oFono's IMS call
property, and imsChanged follows a handover between the two (SRVCC).
Providers that cannot tell keep the default, false.

It reaches clients in the call's D-Bus properties (getProperties'
isIms, and imsChanged) and as VoiceCallHandler.isIms in QML, so the
phone app can show "VoLTE" for a call.

tst_ofonoprovider and tst_dbusservice test it. The cppcheck baseline
entry for the oFono handler's constructor moves a line down.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
